  "summary": "Stack buffer over-read (CWE-125) in LibreSSL 3.4.0 reachable through X.509 name-constraint email handling. x509_constraints_parse_mailbox() copies the mailbox address into a fixed 256-byte stack buffer one character at a time, but the per-character index guard is off by one, so a mailbox whose domain part is exactly 256 characters long fills the entire buffer with no room left for a terminating NUL byte. When the parser then calls strdup() on that buffer it scans past the end of the stack array looking for a NUL, reading adjacent stack memory beyond the object. This is triggered while validating a certificate or mailbox against email name constraints. Affects the libressl 3.4.0 package."
